Linear measurements do not, de-facto, increase discrimination among groups, or better assign individuals to groups.  That is data-specific.

And even with CVA you will still have the incommensurate units and scale to worry about in terms of interpretability of the dataspace. That is inescapable. Conversion to standard normal deviates helps as I stated before.

Dean

